   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "2 damage to the opponent on every instant/sorcery, which Niv-Mizzet, Visionary turns into two cards. The owner kept Spectacular Skywhale; suggested cuts: Paradigm Shifter (a 3-drop dork; its spellbook card is a one-time value), or Saheeli, Jewel of Avishkar.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Improvisation Capstone": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "Free casts off the top until MV 4+, then (paradigm) a free copy of itself every first main phase: a repeating engine Vivi's mana pays for once. Suggested cut: Wanda's Vision (a free cast on the second spell, which Capstone does in bulk); or Zaffai and the Tempests.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Planetarium of Wan Shi Tong": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "{1},{T}: scry 2, then cast the top card free — a free spell every turn from its own ability, more with Temple of Epiphany and Prismari Charm's surveil. Suggested cut: Charred Foyer (plays the top card each upkeep, but you pay for it); or Expressive Iteration.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Sunbird's Invocation": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "Every spell cast from hand cascades into a free one (a second Vivi trigger). Suggested cut: Zaffai and the Tempests (one free hand cast a turn, on a 7-drop); or Wanda's Vision.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Shark Typhoon": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "An X/X flying Shark per noncreature spell, sized by its mana value; can be cycled for a card instead. Suggested cut: Saheeli, Jewel of Avishkar (a 1/1 Thopter per noncreature spell — the same job, smaller). Ovika does Shark's job too, if you would rather keep Saheeli.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Jin-Gitaxias, Progress Tyrant": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "Copies your first artifact/instant/sorcery each turn and counters the opponent's first one each turn: protection and a copy engine in one card. Suggested cut: Teferi, Mage of Zhalfir (also stops instant-speed answers, at {U}{U}{U}); or Melek, or Prismari, the Inspiration (the other 7-drop copy engine).",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  },
  "Kraum, Violent Cacophony": {
   "group": "Candidates",
   "text": "A flier that draws and grows on your second spell every turn — repeatable card flow. Suggested cut: Twinned Vision (two casts, three cards, once); or Firemind's Research, or Expressive Iteration.",
   "graded_at": {
    "103": "8e993e2e7c30"
   }
  }
 },
